{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1530066-simplify-the-rules-for-wraith20","id":1530066,"title":"Simplify the Rules for Wraith20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-05T18:28:00-08:00","id":1530066,"title":"Simplify the Rules for Wraith20","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How would you simplify the rules for Wraith 20?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rules are complicated, so how do you (or how would you) house rule it to make things simpler and quicker? That is, without compromising the themes of the game.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T04:34:17-07:00","id":1537684,"title":"","content":"I would at least borrow the streamlined basic mechanics from V5 for the task resolution.<br /> Which is, the fixated difficulty for each die rolled is 6 and the difficulty of a task is the pure number of successes instead of both.<br /> Each task in the old book would be converted this way:<br /> Difficulty 5 = 1 success difficulty<br /> Difficulty 6 = 2 success difficulty<br /> Difficulty 7 = 3 success difficulty<br /> Difficulty 8 = 4 success difficulty<br /> Difficulty 9 = 5 success difficulty<br /> Difficulty 10 = 6 success difficulty<br /> <br /> It makes some stuff much more difficult (the difficulty 9 and 10 stuff), but a single willpower spent makes you reroll three dice. Still difficult though. But for most stuff it works.<br /> Also get ride of the overly complicated rules for combat, the three types of damage and the damage and soaking rolls, and handle combat rounds mostly like the other kind of actions and task.<br /> <br /> For example overcoming with bare hands a relatively common opponent physically isn't a contested roll but a single roll against a difficulty of two successes, overcoming a more difficult enemy is three, and so on.<br /> <br /> You then have to decide how to handle the pathos and angst mechanics. I don't remember them exactly right now, but it shouldn't be too difficult.<br /> You can expand the mechanic of the shadow die into something towards the hunger mechanics of V5 if you want, but I suggest less punitive results in case of 'bestial failure'.<br /> <br /> All in all I think the V5 basic rules are a good start. Just my personal opinion but I feel the basic mechanics were where the classic ruleset was unnecessarily cluncky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T18:00:02-07:00","id":1537736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1530066-simplify-the-rules-for-wraith20?p=1537684#post1537684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All in all I think the V5 basic rules are a good start. Just my personal opinion but I feel the basic mechanics were where the classic ruleset was unnecessarily cluncky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but not for a 20th Anniversary book.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the X20 line is to just have adjustments while remaining compatible with previous editions and each other.<br /> <br /> However good the V5 rules are, they're good for an eventual Wr5, not a Wr20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T02:19:36-07:00","id":1537748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1530066-simplify-the-rules-for-wraith20?p=1537736#post1537736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but not for a 20th Anniversary book.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the X20 line is to just have adjustments while remaining compatible with previous editions and each other.<br /> <br /> However good the V5 rules are, they're good for an eventual Wr5, not a Wr20.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point might be that but the matter was how to simplify it, to play with it today.<br /> So I don't understand your reply. It sounds like &quot;the whole point is to play it as it is written&quot;, which feels in opposition to what we're aiming for and I don't understand why.<br /> <br /> I didn't say to adopt the V5 rules completely, but to use them as a basis.<br /> The question was how we would simplify the rules, and that's how I would go.<br /> The X20 line is as much clunky as the old storyteller system ever was in my opionion, the differences are too minor.<br /> To simplify such a ruleset you have to change it, I personally feel there is no other way.<br /> <br /> And it starts with the unnecessarily complicated task resolution mechanic.<br /> And in this way trying to avoid to change and rework all the special powers of the various splats, because that would be too much work and not worth it.<br /> <br /> Changing the task resolution mechanic is the fastest way to simplify without having to change everything.<br /> <br /> Other solutions for this can be adopted, of course.<br /> I'm simply of the opinion that V5 offered a semplification in this regard within a system that uses a similar way to handle the character sheet.<br /> <br /> As an alternative it can be &quot;roll a single d10, add the attribute score + the skill score and see if you reach or surpass a number difficulty class&quot; a la current D&amp;D.<br /> It would remove the degrees of success though, which are a basis on which much things work.<br /> <br /> The options for task resolution mechanics out there are many.<br /> I just stand on my opinion that the biggest thing that can be simplified is the rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Ever since the Followers of Set rebranded themselves as The Ministry, I can barely keep a straight face around them.&quot; - Ramona","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15944-ravnos","name":"Ravnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15944_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}